# Most importantly: I'd add a tile-load diagnostic

This is the bit I think we've been missing.

Right now the code says:

> "I successfully created a Leaflet map."

But it doesn't tell us:

> "The map tiles actually arrived."

I'd change the tile layer to:

```javascript
var tileLayer = L.tileLayer(
    'https://{s}.tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png',
    {
        attribution: '&copy; OpenStreetMap contributors',
        maxZoom: 19,
        tileSize: 256
    }
);

tileLayer.on('tileload', function () {
    console.log('MAP TILE LOADED');
});

tileLayer.on('tileerror', function (e) {
    console.error('MAP TILE ERROR:', e);
});

tileLayer.addTo(window.map);
```

That gives us a **binary answer**.

If the browser console says:

```text
MAP TILE LOADED
```

then the network is working and we're looking at a rendering/layout problem.

If it says:

```text
MAP TILE ERROR
```

then **we stop touching Leaflet layout code** and investigate the tile request/network/CDN/browser issue.

That's a much better debugging strategy.

